  "analyst_note": {
    "summary": "SpaceX asks to bolt a mobile-satellite service system onto the Gen2 constellation in the 1.5/1.6 GHz and 1.6/2.4 GHz bands, which is the spectrum play behind expanding direct-to-device service beyond the T-Mobile PCS band. The application revives a request the Space Bureau previously dismissed without prejudice, argues the dismissal was made in error, and picks a direct sharing fight with Globalstar in the Big LEO band, contending the incumbent's legacy CDMA systems use only 0.3 percent of the spectrum they hold.",
    "key_points": [
      "Bands sought: 1525-1559 MHz, 1626.5-1660.5 MHz, 1610-1617.775 MHz, 2483.5-2500 MHz",
      "Modification of the existing Gen2 NGSO authorization (call sign S3069), not a new system",
      "Frames direct-to-device MSS as a 6G-era strategic priority for consumers, critical industries and first responders",
      "Explicitly targets Globalstar's exclusivity in the 1.6/2.4 GHz band, citing 0.3 percent utilization of legacy capacity"
    ],
    "source_doc": "Narrative.pdf",
